    "seconds": 20,
    "summary": "The anomaly is mitigated: `user-service` is running again, and every pod in `test-social-network` is 1/1 Running.\n\n**What I found**\n- The `user-service` pod was stuck in `Pending`, and the deployment showed `0/1` available.\n- The scheduler reported a node affinity/selector mismatch.\n- The deployment had `nodeSelector: kubernetes.io/hostname: extra-node`. No node has that hostname; the only worker is `kind-worker`.\n- The other 25 deployments have no node selector.\n\n**What I changed**\n- Removed the `nodeSelector` from the `user-service` deployment with a JSON patch. I did not add a label to any node.\n- The rollout completed. The new pod `user-service-6d5985bd55-kzfsr` runs on `kind-worker` at 10.244.1.40. Its endpoint is registered on port 9090, and its logs show the server starting.\n\n**Caveats**\n- Helm isn't installed in this shell, so I could not inspect the chart values. If the release is upgraded from the chart, the `nodeSelector` may come back. The chart source should be fixed to match.\n- I did not run an end-to-end functional test (post, timeline, follow) through nginx-thrift. The health check was the pod status, endpoints, and logs.",
